From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tu: Allow preemption on a6xx and expose the realtime queue
 priority

Turnip sets MSM_SUBMITQUEUE_ALLOW_PREEMPT on a7xx+ only, so on a6xx the
kernel never preempts inside a queue's IB list even when it runs several
rings (drm/msm can now preempt on A690). Drop the chip >= 7 check and rely
on has_preemption, the probe for whether the kernel accepts the flag. The
a6xx command stream paths that survive preemption are already in place
for the KGSL backend. (drm/msm also accepts the flag on a single ring when
preemption is turned off with enable_preemption=0; the queue then simply
never gets preempted.)

With several rings the kernel exposes nr_rings * 3 priority levels.
Advertise VK_QUEUE_GLOBAL_PRIORITY_REALTIME when there are at least four
levels; it maps to the highest ring, so a compositor asking for realtime
lands above normal apps. With a single ring (three levels) nothing
changes.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc      | 5 ++++-
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc | 7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
index b42510d..0f84e70 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -1954,7 +1954,10 @@ tu_physical_device_get_global_priority_properties(const struct tu_physical_devic
       return;
    }
 
-   props->priorityCount = MIN2(pdevice->submitqueue_priority_count, 3);
+   /* REALTIME only makes a difference when the kernel has a higher ring to
+    * put it on, i.e. more than one ring's worth of priority levels.
+    */
+   props->priorityCount = MIN2(pdevice->submitqueue_priority_count, 4);
    switch (props->priorityCount) {
    case 1:
       props->priorities[0] = VK_QUEUE_GLOBAL_PRIORITY_MEDIUM_KHR;
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc
index 7cbc2d5..0e6c6da 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc
@@ -341,8 +341,11 @@ msm_submitqueue_new(struct tu_device *dev, struct tu_queue *queue)
       assert(queue->priority >= 0 &&
              queue->priority < dev->physical_device->submitqueue_priority_count);
       struct drm_msm_submitqueue req = {
-         .flags = (dev->physical_device->info->chip >= 7 &&
-                   dev->physical_device->has_preemption ?
+         /* The kernel accepts this flag only when it has more than one
+          * ring, i.e. supports preemption; the a6xx paths that keep state
+          * valid across preemption are shared with the KGSL backend.
+          */
+         .flags = (dev->physical_device->has_preemption ?
                    MSM_SUBMITQUEUE_ALLOW_PREEMPT : 0),
          .prio = queue->priority,
       };
